config SUSFS
	tristate "Sandboxed Userspace FileSystem (SUSFS) support"
	depends on FUSE_FS
	help
	  SUSFS (Sandboxed Userspace FileSystem) is a FUSE-based filesystem that
	  lets unprivileged applications run an isolated userspace filesystem
	  inside a dedicated mount namespace (e.g. for DroidSpace containers).

	  This option registers the SUSFS kernel-side filesystem type. The
	  actual filesystem logic is implemented by the userspace SUSFS daemon,
	  which communicates with the kernel through /dev/fuse (CONFIG_FUSE_FS).

	  To build as a loadable module, choose M here: the module will be called
	  susfs.

	  If unsure, say N.
